      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Coding</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Stack &amp; queue</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Stacks and Queues: Matching, Cancelling, Calculators and Monotonic Order</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">A stack is the right tool whenever the newest unfinished thing must be finished first: an open bracket waiting for its closer, a number waiting for its operator, an outer string waiting for its inner part, an element waiting for something bigger. This page builds each of those uses from one push/pop loop, with steppers, tested templates in Go, C++, Java and Python, and an introduction to the monotonic stack and the monotonic deque.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-monotonic-stack\">Monotonic stack</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-monotonic-deque\">Monotonic deque</a>.</p>\r\n",
